\doxysubsubsection{\texorpdfstring{text\_frame()}{text\_frame()}}
{\footnotesize\ttfamily void text\+\_\+frame (\begin{DoxyParamCaption}\item[{std\+::vector$<$ \mbox{\hyperlink{structvertex3D}{vertex3D}} $>$ \&}]{vector\+\_\+input,  }\item[{std\+::vector$<$ uint $>$ \&}]{nb\+\_\+glyphs,  }\item[{\mbox{\hyperlink{structvertex3D}{vertex3D}} \&}]{offset,  }\item[{\mbox{\hyperlink{structvertex2D}{vertex2D}} \&}]{padding }\end{DoxyParamCaption})}



This method is to calculate the coordinates of each glyphs to be displayed in vertex\+\_\+3D a vector of \mbox{\hyperlink{structvertex3D}{vertex3D}}. It first gets the min and max values for each text element of the \mbox{\hyperlink{classMDE}{M\+DE}} to be displayed and stores them in 2 vectors bottom\+\_\+left\+\_\+front and top\+\_\+right\+\_\+back. It then uses these two vectors and calls \mbox{\hyperlink{text_8h_a4e1bd82ff5f0e3f821efdc438d638ed8}{create\+\_\+vector()}} to fill-\/in vector\+\_\+input. Next in the process it calls \mbox{\hyperlink{group__group__init_gabde5ff272ceb5c53880ed068a10b265c}{init\+\_\+vectors()}} and then \mbox{\hyperlink{group__group__init_ga11a2aa40ef1cca9e941f47ceec84d95d}{init\+\_\+box()}} to initialise G\+PU buffers for display of the text\textquotesingle{}s backgound 3d box. 

